Must Have Multiple of 8 Sectors in Volume

// Disk Format
Sector 0: Filesystem Information
    [Offset, Length] Field

    [0, 64] Bitmap Entry
    [64, 64] Root Directory Entry
    [128, 384] Reserved

Sectors 1 to b: Bitmap

Sectors b+1 to a: Data (Start with Root Directory)

// Directory Entry
[Offset, Length] Field


[0, 29] Name
[29, 1] Flags: 0x01 = Valid Entry, 0x02 = Directory, 0x04 = Executable, 0x08 = Device, 0x10 = Read Only, 0x20 = Top Level, 0x40 = User Readable, 0x80 = User Writable (Overrided by Read Only)
[30, 2] Last Sector Bytes Used 
[32, 4] Start LBA
[36, 4] Length in Sectors
[40, 8] Created Date Unix Time
[48, 8] Modified Date
[56, 8] Accessed Date (Non Applicable for Directories)